  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 messages, 3 patients). Results that came in during the work were reviewed (§7), and three decisions were corrected.\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: first renewed (mr-t0001) on the valid 1/20/26 BMP (K 4.5); the hemolyzed outside K 5.9 was excluded and a repeat BMP ordered (sr-t0002). An outside BMP from 10/20/26 then arrived with a valid K of 5.8. CORRECTED: mr-t0001 cancelled, so lisinopril is not refilled. Prior order mr-00283 stays stopped. Urgent PCP task task-t0020 (focus mr-00283); it also flags the open repeat BMP sr-t0002. Corrected message sent to the patient. Note doc-t0027.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price: metformin 1000 mg BID renewed 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0006). This covers the patient message, the pharmacy request and a second pharmacy request that arrived later. Corrected eGFR 58; HbA1c 7.1% on 8/19/26. Lisinopril 20 mg was first renewed (mr-t0005). The 10/6 creatinine was then corrected to 1.49, a 35.5% rise within 4 weeks of the dose increase, which counts as K ≥5.5. CORRECTED: mr-t0005 cancelled; mr-00295 stays stopped. Urgent PCP task task-t0021 (focus mr-00295). Corrected message sent. Note doc-t0028.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb: metformin 500 mg BID renewed 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0013). eGFR 92; the eGFR of 39 was entered in error; HbA1c 6.9% on 9/28/26. Lisinopril was first given as a 30-day / 0-refill bridge with a BMP ordered (no BMP within 12 months). A valid BMP from 10/22/26 (K 4.6) then arrived. CORRECTED: replaced with 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0019). Task task-t0022 asks to cancel the now-redundant BMP order sr-t0012, since I have no tool to cancel a ServiceRequest. Update sent to the patient. Note doc-t0029.\n\nAll message items are completed. The results queue was not part of this request and was left alone, including the three arrival items, which were reviewed and acted on above.",
